# ─── Desktop build target ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite inlines VITE_* at BUILD time, so whatever is set here is compiled into
# the installer and cannot be changed afterwards by the person running it.
#
# `.env` points at http://localhost:3000 for `npm run dev`. That value was also
# ending up in release builds, so an installed desktop app looked for a backend
# on the user's own machine and could never reach the shared room state — the
# web and desktop could not collaborate at all off the developer's laptop.
#
# Vite loads `.env.production` after `.env` for `vite build`, so this overrides
# it for releases only and leaves local development untouched.
VITE_WEB_URL=https://docusync-dusky.vercel.app
